{"title":"What could Terra and Aqua see? Central Kalimantan, 1 Aug to 31 Oct 2015","rule":"Each cell is 0.01 degree (about 1.1 km) and takes the class of the MODIS 1 km pixel at its centre. A cell-day is: FIRE when Terra or Aqua classed it fire (FireMask 7, 8 or 9) or a VIIRS hotspot shown on the map falls in it; TRUSTED ZERO when there was no fire and at least one of Terra or Aqua saw clear land (FireMask 5); BLIND ZERO when there was no fire, neither saw clear land and at least one saw cloud (FireMask 4); NO DATA when neither had a usable look (not processed 0 to 2, or unknown 6). FireMask is a daily composite of every Terra (or Aqua) pass that day, day and night, keeping the highest class, so one clear pass is enough for clear land, and an \"unknown\" pass can hide a clear one. Cells that were water (FireMask 3) on more days than they were clear land are left out. Blind share = blind zeros / (trusted zeros + blind zeros). Only cells inside the 14 districts are counted. Thick smoke can be classed as cloud; thinner smoke is classed as clear land, and a fire under it may or may not be detected. A trusted zero is not proof that nothing burned: small or smouldering peat fires can stay below the detection limit.","grid":{"bbox":[110.7,-3.6,115.9,0.9],"step_deg":0.01,"width":520,"height":450,"land_cells":123979,"note":"Images are drawn only inside the 14 districts; water cells are left out."},"season":{"F":115619,"T":10649847,"U":619833,"N":20769,"blind":5.5,"daily_blind_median":0.7,"daily_blind_q1":0.1,"daily_blind_q3":4.9,"nodata_pct":0.2,"nodata_from_unknown_pct":0.0,"fire_from_viirs_only_pct":61.2,"one_sensor_only_clear_pct":16.6},"districts":[{"name":"Barito Selatan","F":5716,"T":449790,"U":20617,"N":2645,"blind":4.4},{"name":"Barito Timur","F":2622,"T":241013,"U":10490,"N":163,"blind":4.2},{"name":"Barito Utara","F":2021,"T":706904,"U":32994,"N":1073,"blind":4.5},{"name":"Gunung Mas","F":1841,"T":719260,"U":42427,"N":440,"blind":5.6},{"name":"Kapuas","F":15701,"T"